          "parts": [
            {
              "text": "When dealing with parenting arrangements, custody disputes, and accredited mediation on Brisbane Southside (specifically around **Mount Gravatt** and **Sunnybank**), you generally need two things:\n1. **A registered Family Dispute Resolution Practitioner (FDRP)** to conduct formal mediation and issue a **Section 60I Certificate** (a mandatory requirement before initiating court proceedings under the *Family Law Act 1975*, subject to exceptions).\n2. **A skilled family lawyer** to provide independent advice, draft legally binding Parenting Plans or Consent Orders, and represent you if discussions break down.\n\nBelow are the top recommendations across Mount Gravatt and Sunnybank based on these specific practice areas:\n\n---\n\n### 1. Mount Gravatt: Best for Accredited Mediation & Parenting Law\n\n#### **Life Law Solutions (Mount Gravatt East / Upper Mount Gravatt)**\n* **Why them:** They are one of the very few private practices in the area with an in-house **Registered Family Dispute Resolution Practitioner (FDRP) and Nationally Accredited Mediator** (Fraser Murray) who can formally mediate parenting disputes and issue Section 60I certificates.\n* **Parenting focus:** Principal Elizabeth Fairon and the team focus extensively on child-focused arrangements, formalising parenting agreements, and keeping matters out of court whenever possible.\n* **Best for:** Parents looking for a complete end-to-end service—from accredited mediation to drafting legally binding Consent Orders.\n\n#### **Relationships Australia Queensland – Upper Mount Gravatt Centre**\n* **Location:** 23 Sanders Street, Upper Mount Gravatt\n* **Why them:** If you are seeking government-subsidised or cost-effective Family Dispute Resolution, this is the official **Family Relationship Centre (FRC)** servicing the Brisbane Southside.\n* **Services:** They provide accredited FDRPs, child-inclusive mediation, and Section 60I certificates. While they do not provide personal legal advocacy, they are often the recommended first stop for low-to-medium conflict parenting agreements.\n\n#### **Gullickson Lawyers (Mount Gravatt / Southside)**\n* **Why them:** Principal Sherri Gullickson brings extensive dual expertise as a family court litigator and an accredited Family Dispute Resolution Practitioner. \n* **Parenting focus:** They handle complex child custody negotiations, parental responsibility agreements, and court representation in the Federal Circuit and Family Court of Australia (FCFCOA) if out-of-court dispute resolution fails.\n* **Best for:** High-conflict custody disputes where independent, assertive legal advocacy or legally assisted mediation is needed.\n\n---\n\n### 2. Sunnybank: Best for Custody Disputes & Multicultural Advocacy\n\n#### **Times Lawyers (Sunnybank)**\n* **Location:** Near Sunnybank Market Square / Mains Road\n* **Why them:** A premier Sunnybank practice widely trusted for navigating sensitive family breakdowns. They are particularly valuable for Southside clients requiring bilingual services (English and Mandarin).\n* **Parenting focus:** They advise on children’s living arrangements, schooling, relocation disputes, and parental rights under Australian Family Law. They assist with negotiations and court appearances when parents cannot reach common ground.\n* **Best for:** Local, face-to-face legal guidance and culturally responsive family dispute representation.\n\n#### **Denovo Lawyers (Sunnybank Hills)**\n* **Why them:** Located just minutes from Sunnybank, Denovo Lawyers has built a strong southside reputation for approachable, practical dispute resolution.\n* **Parenting focus:** They regularly assist separating parents with negotiating parenting schedules, handling contravention applications (when one parent breaches existing orders), and formalising Consent Orders.\n\n#### **KLS Legal (Sunnybank)**\n* **Location:** McCullough Street, Sunnybank\n* **Why them:** Offers practical family law services addressing separation, domestic violence matters, and parenting plans. \n* **Best for:** Accessible, practical advice on initial parenting arrangements and out-of-court negotiations.\n\n---\n\n### 3. Dedicated Specialist Representation (Servicing Mount Gravatt & Sunnybank)\n\n#### **Australian Family Lawyers (AFL) – Brisbane South**\n* **Why them:** A national, dedicated family law firm with accredited family law specialists regularly servicing Southside clients.\n* **Focus:** They specialise heavily in contested parenting cases, relocation disputes, and representing parents inside mediation rooms. Over 95% of their matters resolve through negotiation/mediation rather than court trials.\n\n---\n\n### Recommended Next Steps for Your Situation\n\n1. **If you haven’t mediated yet:** Contact an accredited FDRP—such as **Fraser Murray at Life Law Solutions** or the **Relationships Australia Centre in Upper Mount Gravatt**—to arrange an intake session and determine whether mediation or a Section 60I certificate is appropriate.\n2. **If you need independent legal advice during mediation:** Speak to a local specialist (such as **Times Lawyers** in Sunnybank or **Gullickson Lawyers** in Mount Gravatt) prior to your session to clarify what parenting schedule is realistic and legally defensible under the *best interests of the child* principle.\n3. **If you already have an agreement:** Engage a family lawyer to draft and file **Application for Consent Orders** with the court, which gives your agreement the same legal weight as a judge's ruling.",
